<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computing Watermark Robustness (WR) under Dual-Space Smoothing.</span>
Given a text input <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{U},\bm{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{U},\bm{W})</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the prediction distribution (PD) of model <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot;w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot;w)</annotation></semantics></math> as the predicted class-probability distribution under dual-space noise <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\rho},\bm{\varepsilon})\!\sim\!\mathcal{P}_{\bm{\rho},\bm{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜺</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\rho},\bm{\varepsilon})\!\sim\!\mathcal{P}_{\bm{\rho},\bm{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\!\sim\!\mathcal{U}[-\lambda,\lambda]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\!\sim\!\mathcal{U}[-\lambda,\lambda]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\perp\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\perp\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry of the PD is defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}\!\big((\bm{U},\bm{W})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\mathbb{P}_{(\rho,\varepsilon)}\!\Big(\arg\max g\big(\psi(\bm{U},\rho)\cdot\phi(\bm{W},\varepsilon);w\big)=k\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}\!\big((\bm{U},\bm{W})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\mathbb{P}_{(\rho,\varepsilon)}\!\Big(\arg\max g\big(\psi(\bm{U},\rho)\cdot\phi(\bm{W},\varepsilon);w\big)=k\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In practice, PD is approximated via Monte Carlo sampling:</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\small p_{k}\!\big((\bm{U},\bm{W})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\approx\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{I}\!\Big\{\arg\max g\big(\psi(\bm{U},\rho_{i})\cdot\phi(\bm{W},\varepsilon_{i});w\big)=k\Big\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑼</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑾</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≈</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi></munderover><mpadded style="width:0.239em;" width="0.239em"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">arg</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ψ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑼</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑾</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\small p_{k}\!\big((\bm{U},\bm{W})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\approx\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mathbb{I}\!\Big\{\arg\max g\big(\psi(\bm{U},\rho_{i})\cdot\phi(\bm{W},\varepsilon_{i});w\big)=k\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho_{i},\varepsilon_{i})\!\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\!\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho_{i},\varepsilon_{i})\!\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\!\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}\{\cdot\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}\{\cdot\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">From each class, we select one correctly classified clean instance <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and generate its watermarked version <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k},\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k},\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> through the procedure in Section <a href="#S4" title="4. The Proposed Mrthod ‣ DSSmoothing: Toward Certified Dataset Ownership Verification for Pre-trained Language Models via Dual-Space Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, where <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k}=\phi(\bm{W}_{k},\Delta_{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k}=\phi(\bm{W}_{k},\Delta_{e})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k}=\psi(\bm{U}_{k},\Delta_{\rho})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k}=\psi(\bm{U}_{k},\Delta_{\rho})</annotation></semantics></math> denote deterministic trigger injection satisfying <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k}-\bm{W}_{k}\|_{F}&lt;r_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k}-\bm{W}_{k}\|_{F}&lt;r_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k}-\bm{U}_{k}\|_{1}&lt;r_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k}-\bm{U}_{k}\|_{1}&lt;r_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The watermark robustness (WR) of a suspicious model <math id="S4.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot;\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot;\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\!\big(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\min_{k=1,\ldots,K}\ \mathbb{P}_{(\rho,\varepsilon)}\!\Big(\arg\max f\big(\psi(\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k},\rho)\cdot\phi(\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k},\varepsilon);\bm{\theta}\big)=\hat{y}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.913em;" width="0.913em"><mi>W</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\!\big(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\min_{k=1,\ldots,K}\ \mathbb{P}_{(\rho,\varepsilon)}\!\Big(\arg\max f\big(\psi(\widehat{\bm{U}}_{k},\rho)\cdot\phi(\widehat{\bm{W}}_{k},\varepsilon);\bm{\theta}\big)=\hat{y}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This metric quantifies the lowest confidence at which the watermark remains effective across all classes, thereby reflecting its worst-case robustness under dual-space perturbations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ownership Verification via Dual-Space Conformal Prediction.</span>
After computing the WR value, we introduce the principal probability (PP) to measure the prediction stability of benign models under dual-space noise. For a benign model <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot;w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot;w)</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample one correctly classified instance <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> per class and obtain its average prediction distribution <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{p}\!\big((\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\!=\![p_{1},\ldots,p_{K}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi>𝒑</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{p}\!\big((\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\!=\![p_{1},\ldots,p_{K}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The PP is defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\!\big(g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\left\|\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bm{p}\!\big((\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\right\|_{\infty}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.611em;" width="0.611em"><mi>P</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi>𝒑</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑼</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\!\big(g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)=\left\|\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bm{p}\!\big((\bm{U}_{k},\bm{W}_{k})\mid g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)\right\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the maximum norm, representing the average confidence of benign models on the most probable class.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We then compute PP values across <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> benign models trained on non-protected datasets to form the calibration set <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}\!=\!\{P_{C}^{1},\ldots,P_{C}^{J}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>J</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}\!=\!\{P_{C}^{1},\ldots,P_{C}^{J}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since these PP values may exhibit heavy-tailed distributions due to dataset shift, we apply outlier filtering: given a ratio <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\!\in\![0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\!\in\![0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the largest <math id="S4.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!=\!\lfloor\kappa J\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!=\!\lfloor\kappa J\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> PP values are discarded to avoid overly conservative thresholds.
Based on this, we compare the WR value of the suspicious model with the PP values in the calibration set and compute a decision threshold under a chosen significance level. Ownership verification is then formalized as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_theorem">Proposition 0 (Ownership Verification via Dual-Space Conformal Prediction).</h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}=\{P_{C}^{1},\ldots,P_{C}^{J}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>J</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}=\{P_{C}^{1},\ldots,P_{C}^{J}\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the PP values in the calibration set, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=W(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=W(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the WR value of the suspicious model. The suspicious model is considered to be trained on the protected dataset <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\!\big(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)&gt;P_{C}^{(J-m-\lfloor\alpha_{0}(J-m+1)\rfloor)}(g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.913em;" width="0.913em"><mi>W</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\!\big(f_{\bm{\theta}},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}\big)&gt;P_{C}^{(J-m-\lfloor\alpha_{0}(J-m+1)\rfloor)}(g_{w},\mathcal{P}_{\rho,\varepsilon}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the calibration set, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\lfloor\kappa\cdot J\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\lfloor\kappa\cdot J\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of filtered outliers, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the filtering ratio, and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e.g." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e.g.</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>) is the significance level. In addition, <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}^{(j)}(g_{w},\mathcal{P}{\rho,\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}^{(j)}(g_{w},\mathcal{P}{\rho,\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th smallest element in the calibration set <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{C}(\mathcal{P}{\rho,\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{C}(\mathcal{P}{\rho,\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> constructed from benign models <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span>Performance (%) of dataset watermarking (BA, WSR) and ownership verification (VSR, WCA) on SST-2 dataset with BERT, OPT-1.3B, and GPT-2 under three noise levels (0.02, 0.03, 0.04). Best verification results are in bold.</figcaption>
