</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13. </span>WSR of our method’s watermarked samples on the AG dataset under perturbations in the embedding space. <math id="A8.F13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.F13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the noise and adversarial directions, respectively, and ‘<math id="A8.F13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bullet" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∙</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bullet</annotation></semantics></math>’ marks the original watermarked sample. Left: BadWord. Right: AddSent.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A8.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A8.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15303v1/heatmap_AG_VSR.png" id="A8.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:105/88;" width="105" height="88" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F14.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A8.F14.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">AG (VSR)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A8.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.15303v1/heatmap_AG_WCA.png" id="A8.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:105/88;" width="105" height="88" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F14.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A8.F14.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">AG (WCA)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14. </span>Performance on AG with different benign (rows) and watermarked (columns) model architectures.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Model-level Transferability on AG Dataset</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A8.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Appendix H Effects of the Number of Benign Models ‣ DSSmoothing: Toward Certified Dataset Ownership Verification for Pre-trained Language Models via Dual-Space Smoothing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> shows the results on the AG dataset. The overall trends are consistent with those observed on SST-2, demonstrating that DDSmoothing remains effective across different architectures.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A10" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix J </span>Societal Impacts</h2>

<div id="A10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This paper focuses on protecting public datasets used in pre-trained language model (PLM) training. We identify that existing dataset ownership verification (DOV) methods are vulnerable to perturbations and propose a robust, certifiable approach that enables privacy-preserving and traceable ownership verification. The method is purely defensive, aiming to promote fair data usage, trustworthy sharing, and responsible AI development. Although it employs a trigger-based watermarking mechanism similar in form to backdoor attacks, its use is strictly limited to legitimate and authorized verification scenarios. When applied in controlled and compliant environments, it introduces <em id="A10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no additional</em> security or privacy risks, thereby contributing positively to trustworthy data governance and the sustainable development of transparent AI systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
